 * restrictTries (Patricia co-descent) — restriction was a top hot op (datalog `edges<|nbs`, aunt,
   sliding). geomean 1.990 -> 1.679.
 * joinAll balanced-pairwise-union (de-boxed; was mutable.HashMap[Int(boxed),ArrayBuffer]) — used by
   tailsUnion (datalog `⋁`) and evalI iteration. geomean 1.679 -> 1.526.
WARM ABLATION (all 10 benchmarks, steady-state comp+run geomean ms):
  baseline(both off)=6.287 | +literalByRef only=2.150 | +patriciaOps only=5.666 | ALL=1.526
  => literal-by-ref 2.92x alone; full Patricia trie ops add the rest; ALL = 4.12x. Target 1.257 (5x).
Remaining dominators: datalog80 ~12.4 (bilinear cumulative Fixpoint — semi-naive needs the non-linear
product rule, deferred as high-risk), n-queens compile (push_out LICM 2-3ms), nq7 run.

--- MEASUREMENT METHODOLOGY + FINAL ABLATION (steady-state, warm compile + warm run, min-of-trials) ---
The op-graph compile was being measured COLD (once) while run was warm best-of-N — inconsistent and
noisy (a cold compile mostly measures JIT warmup; nq6 compile 11ms cold vs ~3.7ms warm). Fixed: warm
the compile path (3 builds) before the profiled one, like the run column. Added Tuning.{literalByRef,
patriciaOps} toggles (default ON) for clean attribution; GraphBench now prints comp+run AND run-only
geomeans tagged with the active config.

DEFINITIVE WARM ABLATION (10 benchmarks, geomean ms; min over 3 trials shown — machine has ~±15% load noise):
  config                         comp+run   run-only
  baseline (both off)              ~4.26      ~0.335
  +literalByRef only               ~1.71      ~0.38   (literal fix is COMPILE-only; doesn't touch run)
  +patriciaOps only                ~4.21      ~0.234  (trie ops are RUN-only; 1.4x run alone)
  ALL (optimized)                  ~1.11      ~0.112
  => comp+run ~3.8-4.4x ; run-only ~3.0x.  Attribution: literal-by-ref carries comp+run (2.85x alone,
     kills the temperature literal-serialization); Patricia trie ops carry run-only (restriction + joinAll
     were the real hot ops — restriction 1.99->1.68, joinAll 1.68->1.53 on earlier 2-warmup runs).
HONEST CEILING: ~4x. Remaining levers are NOT low-hanging:
  - n-queens COMPILE (~4ms warm): genuine push_out LICM work over the large inlined place(n,n) graph;
    place() is memoized, allRefs is linear-with-depth — no O(N^2) bug. Only ~1.3x in boxed-Int sets.
  - datalog RUN (Fixpoint): next(m)=m∪step(m) is cumulative AND bilinear (m joined with m); a correct
    semi-naive needs the non-linear product rule + a soundness check — high risk, deferred.
Decision: consolidate the clean ~4x (literal-by-ref + complete IntMap-native trie ops), zero regressions,
full attribution. Deliver GoL grid-as-argument variant + pipeline-stage ablation + writeup.

