[2026-06-27] IterUnion_Indep: fixed the soundness hole WITHOUT removing the rule; +Unwrap∘Unwrap merge; rule audit.
egglog (formal.egg): added an Iter model (Iter src invariant-body = union of body over heads of src;
Empty over a headless source) and CHECKED three facts:
 - distributing a body-union over the iteration is SOUND on empty AND non-empty sources;
 - the BARE hoist is UNSOUND on an empty source (leaks the invariant branch);
 - the bare hoist IS sound when the source is provably HEADED;
 - contrast: hoisting an invariant Wrap out is sound (Wrap absorbs the empty source).
SC fix (Lower.IterUnion_Indep): hoist an invariant union branch OUT (strongest product-whack: branch
computed once, no re-iteration) but GUARD on provablyHeaded(src) — a conservative static "src has >=1
head" test (Singleton/Literal/Union/Wrap of a non-empty/headed sub-space).  When not provably headed we
do NOT rewrite (no bloat, no regression); op-graph push_out still does sound dynamic LICM for the
symbolic case.  Tried unconditional DISTRIBUTE first (also sound) but it regressed idx42 execT 3.8->21.8ms
via re-iteration bloat push_out couldn't recover — the headed-guard avoids that.
New rule Lower.Unwrap_Merge: merge adjacent CONSTANT unwraps into one (egglog-checked).  Constant-only so
it cannot oscillate with UnwrapConcat_Unwraps (the splitter only fires on Concat prefixes; a merged
Constant prefix is immune) -> resolves the 61 surviving Unwrap(Unwrap) cases (now 0%).
Test: Unification."transpile transform" was PINNING the old unsound hoist op-graph (it gated each cux by a
single sub-query, leaking output when another conjunct was empty).  Replaced the brittle op-graph dump
with an eval-equivalence check over partial-match inputs (uses evalI; eval can't grow iteration contexts)
that locks in the conjunctive semantics.
Audit of formal.egg <-> SC: rules correspond and are sound.  Intentional directional differences: SC uses
UnwrapConcat split (Concat-prefix -> nested) as normal form + Unwrap_Merge (nested-constants -> single)
while formal.egg states the general merge; formal.egg (Wrap prefix space) arg order is flipped vs MORKL
Space.Wrap(src, prefix).  formal.egg has selection-pushing distributions (Unwrap/Restriction/Product/
Intersection/Subtraction over Union) NOT in the SC reduce (they are non-monotone; left to driving/push_out).
