2026-07-13  Abstract result-size analysis (Lower.sizeBounds)
================================================================================
Interval abstraction of a space's size: SizeBounds(lo, loHeaded, hi) with
lo <= |eval(s)| <= hi and loHeaded a lower bound on the HEADED path count (the
number of groups an iteration runs).  Transfer functions per constructor,
saturating arithmetic, unknowns (mentions/calls/grounded) widen to [0, inf).
Two corrections over the sketched old attempt, both pinned by tests:
 - intersection upper is min (not max);
 - composition lower is max(lo_l, lo_r) when both sides are nonempty, NOT
   lo_l*lo_r: concatenation splits can collide ({a,aa}.{a,aa} has 3 paths, not
   4).  The product upper stays.
 - iteration lower takes ONE group's body (bodies may overlap across groups),
   gated on loHeaded(src) >= 1 — an eps-only source runs zero groups, so plain
   nonemptiness would be unsound (same refinement as the headedGuard work).
Integration ("get rid of everything superseded"):
 - provablyNonEmpty / provablyHeaded are now one-liners over sizeBounds
   (lo >= 1 / loHeaded >= 1) — the syntactic case enumerations are gone, and
   the guards got strictly stronger (e.g. subtraction of a provably-empty
   right side, Range windows, fixpoint-from-init now prove headedness), so
   IterUnion_Indep hoists bare in more cases.
 - New rule SizeEmpty (hi == 0 => Empty) opens the optimized() pipeline —
   analysis-level empty propagation through arbitrary nesting.
