    nodes are statically evaluable (family@"female" is exactly 4 paths) but
    seeded [0,26]; the intersection, wrap and iteration inherit the slop up to
    hi = 2*26 = 52.  Fix: groundFold in the z3 tier — a node with NO free
    variables (binder-aware freeMentions/freeRefs; no Call/Grounded), budget
    hi <= 200k, is evaluated and seeded with its EXACT size (memoized).  The
    e-pin applies only to actual folds (a syntactic [k,k] seed may still have
    unknown eps — caught during review, would have been unsound).
 2. THE ITERATION UPPER USED ONLY CONSTANT BODY ENDPOINTS.  n_it <= hd*K(body)
    ignores variable-level tightening of the body (n_body <= 4 after folding
    never reached n_it).  Fix: the dual linear form n_it <= K(src)*n_body
    (constant source coefficient, VARIABLE body), sound with the witness
    binding chosen as the argmax-body group; same for Fold.
    Chain on aunt: [0,52] -> (fold family@"female"=4) -> [0,8].
 3. THE REST IS PARTIAL-EVALUATION SLACK, NOT CONSTRAINT SLACK.  [0,8] vs the
    true 1 needs per-group case-splitting: person ranges over the KNOWN
    {Jim, Pam}, but one abstract body variable cannot represent per-group
    variation.  A/B: optimized() unrolls (IterateLiteral_Union) and folds the
    whole program to Literal({Aunt.Jim.Ann}) — both analyses exact [1,1].
    With closedness relaxed to free-variables-only, groundFold reaches the
    root of any closed program: aunt answers [1,1] directly.
