2026-07-14  Open pure GoL drilldown: program, constraints, three findings
================================================================================
SizeZ3Drilldown gained the open-GoL specimen: nextStep+neigh fully inlined
(inlineCalls — Routine.optimized only inlines ONE call level, which is also
why the earlier closed suite row stayed [0,inf)) with S"field" free.
Findings and fixes:
 1. BINDER REUSE BLOCKED ENCODING ENTIRELY: both GoL arms bind x/ys, so the
    program was ScopeLimited ("binder 'ys' names two distinct subtrees") and
    got NO constraints.  Fix: alphaRename pre-pass in SizeZ3 (post-order, so
    shadowing renames inner-first; lengthHints preserved) — encoding now runs
    on the renamed alpha-equivalent term; scopesProblem stays as the residual
    guard (Call arguments are not renamed).
 2. THE exactly-k IDIOM WAS UNBOUNDED: Range(count, k, k+1) is a width-1
    ordered slice, but only (0,k)/(-k,0) windows were special-cased — general
    same-sign windows fell back to [0, hi_src].  Fix in BOTH tiers: width
    <= b - a for same-sign slices.  The per-cell exactly-k chain is now
    provably [0,1] (Range [2,3) -> tee -> subtraction all [0,1]).
 3. THE ROOT [0,inf) FOR OPEN FIELD IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A BUG: the result is
    really <= c*|field@Cell|, but a constant-interval answer language cannot
    express bounds PARAMETRIC in an input's size; the linear system also
    deliberately avoids variable*variable products (hd_src * n_body).
    Parametric (symbolic-coefficient) bounds are the natural next tier.
Closed contrast (glider, 8x8): eval = 5; baseline [0, 146410025] (the
multiplicative nest explosion) vs z3 [1, 257] — ~570,000x tighter, from
