2026-08-06  Cornerstone bound analysis -> SIX improvements to the abstract interpretation
================================================================================
Diagnosed every loose cornerstone bound to a root cause and implemented the fix for each.

(1) SPATIAL GROUND FOLDING (SpatialTypes.groundFold). A closed subterm denotes one fixed set, so
    evaluate it and take the EXACT per-length HISTOGRAM -- strictly more information than SizeZ3's
    exact count, and no solver needed. Consulted at every node before the structural transfers.
(2) WORK-BUDGETED FOLD. The syntactic gate (sizeBounds.hi <= 200k) misses terms whose syntactic
    upper is inf but whose true result is tiny (the expanded 15-puzzle: true size 2, syntactic inf --
    the limitation logged 2026-07-14). Added a fallback: when the syntactic bound is unusable, gate
    on a LITERAL-WEIGHT proxy (total literal paths below the term <= 4000, since every output path is
    built from them) and evaluate under a 150ms wall cap on a DAEMON thread, abandoned if it
    overruns. Any failure returns None and the transfers take over.
(3) FIXPOINT LENGTH via iterate-and-check (Lower.lenBounds). Was hull(init, body) with `rec`
    UNBOUND, so one recursive mention widened every fixpoint to [0, inf). Now Kleene-iterates with
    rec bound to the running candidate and verifies the post-fixpoint condition F(t) subset-of t
    (certified: proofs/spatial/lat_postfixpoint.smt2); unverified falls back to unknown.
(4) INTERPROCEDURAL CALLS in all three analyses. `Lower.sizeBounds(s, rc)`, `Lower.lenBounds(s, rc)`
    and `SpatialEnv(routines = rc)` analyse a Call by binding the callee's parameters to the ARGUMENT
    types (sound: a body denotes a function of its parameters); an `active`/`stack` set stops
    re-entry so recursion widens to unknown instead of diverging. lenBounds also gained a PATH env so
    ref parameters bind (puzzle15's superpose takes a path). The no-rc entries are unchanged, so the
    law guards (provablyNonEmpty/provablyHeaded) behave exactly as before.
(5) rc THREADED INTO BOTH z3 TIERS so their per-node baseline seeds are interprocedural too --
    without this the tier-1 answer could be TIGHTER than the z3 baseline and dominance broke (caught
    immediately by the CornerstoneTypes gate on gol).
(6) SPATIAL now honours SpaceMention.sizeHint (exactly k paths at unknown lengths). It was ignoring
    the hint tier-1 already trusted -- found by re-testing the s||g derivation on an open term.
ALSO a precision bug fixed in `join`: when one side had a spill bucket its paths were materialised
into the output's tracked classes AND left in the output rest -- the same paths twice, which inflated
the certified s||g bracket [2,5] to [2,11]. With a spill present the join now collapses to one bucket
carrying summed totals and the hull of both length ranges.

