4. THE NAMING TRAP IS CLOSED  (finding 1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`satisfies` is DELETED, not deprecated. The carrier agent left it as a @deprecated alias; a
deprecated alias leaves the trap reachable, which is exactly what the review objected to, so I
adapted the two remaining consumers (SpatialLawCheck, SpatialSoundnessHunt) to `withinEnvelope` and
removed the alias. `grep -rn "\bsatisfies("` over src/ is now empty. Full gamma is `accepts`
(alias gammaMember); the weak envelope is `withinEnvelope`.

The envelope's gap is REAL and still measured: 237 non-members admitted over 38,400 pairs, 0 genuine
members rejected. What changed is that NO DISPATCHER IS BUILT ON IT any more —
SpecializedRoutine.applicableTo, BoundedRecursion.applicableTo and
SpatialPipeline.GuardedRoutine.applicableTo all decide with full gamma. A comment in SpatialLawCheck
still claimed the opposite ("applicableTo is built on it, so a guarded dispatcher can select a
specialisation for an input outside the precondition"); that claim was FALSE as of this increment, so
I corrected it and added an assertion that the dispatcher REJECTS the exact witness the envelope
admits, so the claim cannot rot back into being true.

