(A) THE EXECUTORS: YES. Every sharing / whole-subtree case has measured slope 0.00, and the
    improvements are slope changes against the previous implementations, not constant factors
    (OptimalTrieCheck, counted events, geometric ladder 512..8192 or 64..1024):
      restriction by {eps}        touch 1        alloc 0     slope 0.00
      restriction by one prefix   touch 17       alloc 1     slope 0.00  (8 accepted by pointer)
      disjoint union              touch 2        alloc 1     slope 0.00
      subset intersection         touch 3        alloc 0     slope 0.00
      disjoint intersection       touch 2        alloc 0     slope 0.00  (2 rejected by pointer)
      self / disjoint subtraction touch 1 / 2    alloc 0     slope 0.00
      {eps}.B and A.{eps}         touch 1        alloc 0     slope 0.00
      full Range (warm)           touch 1        alloc 0     slope 0.00  BEFORE: 1023..16383, slope 1.00
      joinAll of k disjoint       alloc 1                    slope 0.00  BEFORE: alloc k-1, slope 1.00
      meetAll smallest frontier   touch 19..27   slope 0.14  BEFORE: 2595..41011, slope 1.00
      one-head tailsIntersection  touch 1        alloc 0     slope 0.00
      fused raffination           touch 9 alloc 1            BEFORE: touch 12 alloc 2
      fixpoint equalT (converged) equality 1                 BEFORE: 1023..16383, slope 1.00

(B) THE ESTIMATE, CASE 1 -- RIGHT SLOPE, BAD CONSTANT. LIM-4 recorded predicted `touch` slope
    0.87-0.93 against a measured 0.00 and called it a GROWTH-CLASS error. IT IS NOT, and this is the
    correction I am most confident matters. `SpatialFrontier`'s Patricia term is
    `min(2(fanL+fanR), 2*PatriciaBits*(gateFan+|A|))` with `PatriciaBits = 33`, so the
    operand-INDEPENDENT branch cannot win until the growing fan passes ~33x the gating fan -- and the
    five-rung ladder (64..1024) sits ENTIRELY inside that crossover. Measured out to 65536:
      restrict/prefix-cylinder  pred touch 311, 567, 1079, 1591, then 1591 at SIX more doublings
                                meas 13 flat.   per-doubling slopes 0.86, 0.93, 0.56, 0.00 x 6
      union/subset              pred 216, 408, 792, 1458, then 1458 x 6;  meas 16 -> 26
      inter/shared-subtrie      pred 86 at EVERY rung 64..65536;          meas 26 flat
      absorption (x u x)        pred touch 1, alloc 0;                    meas 1, 0  -- EXACT
    So the whole-subtree accept DOES reach `touch`, the bound IS constant in the operand size, and
    what remains is a constant of 122x / 56x / 3.3x. The user's steer says care about slopes, not
    constants: by that standard this class is DONE. I kept LIM-4 as a failure (122x still fails the
    budget tier) and rewrote its text; I did NOT lengthen the ladder, because changing the rung set
    moves all 129 ladder numbers and can trip a cap in either direction at integration time.

(C) THE ESTIMATE, CASE 2 -- STILL WRONG. Three families are genuinely linear, slope 1.00 at every one
    of ten doublings:
      union/disjoint-keys  pred alloc 66, 130, 258, ..., 65538   meas alloc 2, FLAT       (LIM-5)
      range/full           pred touch 67, 131, ..., 65539        meas touch 1, FLAT       (LIM-3)
      zipper Work/Alloc    pred prop. to Meas.nodes              meas flat, worst 2053x   (LIM-1/2)
    LIM-5's CAUSE IS NOW LOCATED, which LIM-5 did not know. Sweeping keys-per-side upward, the
    frontier reports source `Exact` and a FLAT predicted alloc of 3 for 1..12 keys, then switches to
    `Relational` with 16, 18, 26, 66 at 14, 16, 24, 64. The crossover is
