================================================================================================
SESSION 2026-08-08 (cont) — THE `touch` LOWER ENDPOINT: 62 -> 58 WIDTH FAILURES, AND THREE LATENT
UNSOUND LOWER ENDPOINTS THE OLD POLICY WAS HIDING
================================================================================================
Steer: "Address the analysis side now."  Every one of the 62 per-operator product-requirement
failures in SpatialCostCheck was a WIDTH failure, and all 62 had one cause: `SpatialCost.analyze`
ended with an unconditional `c.withoutTouchLower`, so `touch` was [0, hi] and its width was
`upper + 1` BY CONSTRUCTION.

THE FILE HEADER'S JUSTIFICATION FOR THAT WAS WRONG.  It said the fast paths "can eliminate
essentially every internal visit".  True of the RECURSIVE visits; false of the ENTRY.  `unionR`,
`intersectionR`, `subtractionR`, `restrictionR`, `raffinationR`, `compositionR`, `joinAll`, `meetAll`,
`wrap`, `unwrap`, `tailsUnion`, `tailsIntersection`, `range` and `singleton` each emit their
`TrieNodeVisit` as their FIRST statement -- before `a eq b`, before the `isEmpty` tests, before
everything.  `evalI` is eager (`ITrie.union(evalI(a), evalI(b))` always calls the operation), so one
visit per algebra node cannot be avoided by any data distribution.

WHAT LANDED
  * policy: claim a lower endpoint only where there is an ORACLE to refute it.  `withoutTouchLower`
    now applies only to a model whose `touch` has none -- `ReferenceCost` over Set[PathValue].
  * `TrieAlgebraCost.entryVisit`: one forced visit per algebra node for `evalI`/`execZ`; ZERO for
    `GraphCost`, because `execT` guards every space slot with `if a.isEmpty then empty` and never
    enters the algebra.  The corpus calibration is what established that distinction (see below).
  * `FrontierSyms.descentsLo`: the frontier's MUST-PAIRED count, previously dropped at the Sym
    boundary.  Claimed only under `mustDescend` -- both operands provably non-empty AND provably
    different sets (one's proven minimum size exceeds the other's maximum, so `a eq b` is impossible).
    Only the three SYMMETRIC merges use it: restriction/raffination also short-circuit on `eps in
    right` and composition on `{eps}` on either side, and `Meas` carries neither eps-presence nor a
    LOWER length bound, so their must side stays unclaimed and is recorded as such in OP-1.

THREE LATENT UNSOUND LOWER ENDPOINTS, ALL EXPOSED THE MOMENT THE BLANKET STOPPED HIDING THEM, all
found by the corpus containment gate and not by inspection:
  1. a warm `Literal` claimed `exact(touch = 1)`; `iLiteral` is a memo-cache lookup that never enters
     the algebra, so the actual is ZERO.
  2. `Unwrap` claimed `exact(touch = 1 + |p|)`; `ITrie.unwrap` stops at the first ABSENT item, so a
     missing prefix costs ONE visit.
  3. `group` claimed `exact(touch = heads)`; `evalI`'s Iteration iterates `t.children` and emits
     NOTHING for the split -- the head children ARE the groups.  Witness: `Touch actual=25 in
     [27, 209]` on a two-group loop, overshooting by exactly `heads`.
  Plus `fixStep`, where a per-round forced visit over-claims by one per fixpoint: the round that
  DETECTS convergence runs `equalT` and stops without the accumulating `union`.

MEASURED
  * calibration containment WITH the new lower endpoints: 100.00% (0 of 3000 corpus points outside
    the interval) and 100.00% (0 of 59 cornerstone points).  Three intermediate states on the way
    there, each one a refutation that located a defect: 40 out, then 6 out (all `graph`, which is what
    identified execT's short circuits), then 0.
  * SpatialCostCheck per-operator width failures: 62 -> 58.  Every trie `Touch` width exactly halved
    (restriction/raffination 254 -> 127, composition 138 -> 69, iteration 226 -> 113, tails-union
    221 -> 110.5, tails-inter 1754 -> 877, range-part 273 -> 136.5, fixpoint 56868 -> 28434), and
    `union`, `intersection`, `subtraction` and `range-full` went INSIDE the budget tier outright --
    they left OP-1 by the ledger's own necessity rule.
  * cornerstones: `aunt` trie Touch width 12.99 and `temperature` 24.25 (both inside the budget tier,
    both removed from CS-10); `aunt` zipper 13.11 (removed from CS-11).  On those three the missing
    lower endpoint WAS the whole gap, exactly as the previous revision of CS-10 predicted.  `gol`
    (70.06) and `datalog-sn` (1198) remain and their residue is the UPPER endpoint -- LIM-4's Patricia
    constant and CS-5's fixpoint round bound -- not the lower one.

WHAT IS STILL OPEN, NAMED: the 58 remaining failures.  OP-1's eight surviving operators need their
