## 2026-08-31 — acceptance-review resolution pass, round 1: environment, tool paths, the corpus gate, and a
## soundness bug the widened fuzzer found

TOOLCHAIN, FROM NOTHING.  This machine had no JVM, no sbt, no z3, no vampire and no egglog.  All of
them are now installed under `.tools/` (gitignored) with `.tools/env.sh` putting them on PATH:
Temurin JDK 21.0.12.1, sbt 2.0.8 + scala-cli 1.16.0 via coursier, z3 5.1.0, Vampire 5.1.0, and
egglog 3.0.0 built from source at tag v3.0.0 (needed `apt-get install build-essential` first — there
was no C linker either).  `egglog formal.egg` passes on that build, so the egg models are green
against the current upstream, not only against whatever was installed when they were written.

ITEM 4 — TOOL PATHS.  An absolute macOS prover path (under /Applications) was hardcoded in `proofs/run.sh`,
`proofs/spatial-semantic/run.sh`, `scripts/mine_laws.py` and `EquivPipelineTest`; `z3` and
a cargo-bin egglog were assumed in five more places.  There is now ONE policy in three twins —
`src/main/scala/Tools.scala`, `scripts/toolpath.sh`, `scripts/toolpath.py` — reading `$Z3`,
`$VAMPIRE`, `$EGGLOG`, then PATH, then a short conventional-location list, and every call site goes
through it.  A missing tool is a NAMED error that says which variable to set, never a silent skip
(`docs/traps.md` §3).  Verified end to end: `proofs/run.sh` and `terminating/run.sh` both run on
this machine with no absolute path anywhere.  Four personal absolute paths under a
developer home directory, in the example loaders, were replaced by `$ZIPPY_DATA`.

THE TEST JVM NOW FORKS, AND THAT REVIVED SEVENTEEN DEAD GATES.  Every corpus-wide soundness gate was
failing with

    ClassCastException: cannot assign instance of scala.collection.generic.DefaultSerializationProxy
    to field morkl.SpaceValue.paths of type scala.collection.immutable.Set

Run in-process, sbt's LAYERED test classloader makes `ObjectInputStream.latestUserDefinedLoader`
resolve `DefaultSerializationProxy` in a different layer from `morkl.SpaceValue`, so the proxy's
`readResolve` never runs.  The identifying measurement: the SAME `corpus_1000.ser` reads cleanly
from a plain `java` process started on sbt's own `Test/fullClasspath`.  So it was never an artifact
problem.  `Test / fork := true` (plus `-Xmx24G -Xss16M -Dfile.encoding=UTF-8`, and a `.jvmopts` for
the sbt JVM, whose 1 GB default was OOM-ing six more tests) fixes it, and the twenty hand-rolled
copies of the corpus read are now one `Corpus.load()` that reports ABSENT / STALE / UNREADABLE with
the regeneration command.  Full suite: 37 failures -> 17.

ITEM 6 — THE FUZZER, AND WHAT IT IMMEDIATELY FOUND.  `Raffination` and `TailsIntersection` had ZERO
occurrences in the 1000-program corpus; every one of the seven executors supports both.  Naive
addition is degenerate — an independently drawn raffination subtrahend removes nothing, and a
tails-intersection of an arbitrary source is almost always empty — so the generator draws a PROPER
non-empty subset of the argument's heads for `\|`, and a shared-tail source (`heads x body`) for
tails-intersection one draw in four.  The full-window `Range` (`hi == 0`, the identity window) was
also undrawable and is now 1 in 6.  Regenerated corpus census: Raffination 1371, TailsIntersection
1013, identity Range 91, from 0 / 0 / 0.  `ProgramExpressivity` now ASSERTS that census, because
`FuzzRec`'s `serialVersionUID` does not change when the generator does, so nothing else would have
noticed the corpus going stale.  Four hand-written `nodes` helpers that each missed a different set
of constructors (and one of which IS the corpus accept filter) now call one owner,
`SpatialPipeline.nodeCount`.

AND THE BUG.  On the first run of the new corpus, 10 of 1000 programs produced a supercompiler
residual with a DANGLING binder — `evalI` died with `key not found: PathRef(h418115)`.  Root cause,
minimised to a 6-line term: `collect` (MORKL.scala) had no `Space.Raffination` arm and fell into its
`case x => x` catch-all, so the entire subtree under a `\|` was INVISIBLE to it.  `collect` is the
traversal EVERY loop-invariance test is written in (`IterUnion_Indep`, `IterComposition_Indep`,
`cleanSpace` and through it `IterCompRight_Hoist`), so a body that used an iteration binder under a
raffination looked loop-invariant and was hoisted out of its own binder.  `subs`, `freeMentions`,
`freeRefs` and `SizeZ3.children` were all already total — `collect` alone was not.  This is
`docs/traps.md` §7 verbatim, and it was undetectable for exactly as long as the fuzzer could not
draw the operator: item 6 and this bug are the same finding.  Fixed, and `TraversalTotality` now
puts a marker in every subterm position of every constructor and asserts each traversal sees it, so
a future missing arm is a red test naming the constructor.  `CorpusLawValidation` back to 100000
checks all agreeing.

ITEM 8 — BACKEND SELECTION REMOVED.  `chooseBackend`/`selectBackend`/`BackendChoice` scored
`work + alloc + rounds + touch` at one valuation and took an argmin.  Four separate defects: the sum
adds four components with four different counted oracles and no common unit; only the UPPER endpoint
was compared, so `[1,1000]` "beat" `[900,1001]`; there was no overlap test and no use of
`Sym.dominates`; and it minimised across a DECLARED oracle gap (`ReferenceCost.touchNoOracle` forces
that backend's `touch` lower endpoint to 0).  Replaced by `compareBackends`, which reports the
per-component intervals and states DOMINANCE only when they are disjoint on every component —
`INCOMPARABLE` is the normal, honest answer.  A regression test asserts the argmin API cannot come
back.

ITEM 7 — RANGE COST.  Three stale terms, all removed with the measurement that justifies it.
(a) `IntTrie.ordered`'s per-node key sort emits NO counted event, and `touch` is DEFINED as
`TrieNodeVisit + PatriciaVisit`; charging `2·(len+1)·heads·log(heads)` to it was unmeasurable slack
and the dominant term in `range-part`'s width (144 of a predicted 199 against a counted 7).  It is
now a DECLARED assumption on the report instead.  (b) `slice` is an ORDER-STATISTIC descent: at any
node the window is one contiguous index block and the children are contiguous disjoint blocks, so at
most TWO children are partial and the recursion is two root-to-leaf chains — `O(depth + window)`,
a SUM, not the product `(w+2)(L+1)` charged for both `nodes` and (times `tPer`) `touch`.  (c) `slice`
uses plain `IntMap` ops, not the instrumented `IntTrieOps`, so it emits no `PatriciaVisit` at all and
the `tPer = 3` multiplier does not apply to this operator.  `ZipperCost.range` additionally charged a
QUADRATIC `3·w·(w·L + L + 2)` left over from the path-by-path predecessor, and an unconditional
materialisation walk — `Meas.concrete` (from the already-existing `liftsToLit`) now says when
`materialize` hands back an existing trie.  `GraphCost` recovers its provable lower `touch` of 1:
`GraphExec` has no empty guard for `Range`, which `forcedUnary` already knew and `entryVisit` threw
away.

ITEM 15 — THE WIDTH/DEPTH SPILL NO LONGER CHANGES THE ASYMPTOTIC PREDICTION.  `Shape` gained a FIFTH
γ channel, `otherKeys: Option[Set[PathItem]]` — "every untracked head is named in `ks`", `None` = ⊤ —
minted in `Shape.mk`'s spill and in `capDepth`'s, carried through `weaken`/`openCounts`/`widen`, and
transferred per operator by the head-set image of the operation (union unions, the deleting operators
keep the left operand's, composition grafts, meet intersects).  It is capped by its OWN budget,
`Shape.MaxSpillKeys = 4096`, decoupled from `MaxHeads = 12` because the two bound different things:
`MaxHeads` bounds tracked SUB-SHAPES, this bounds NAMES.  `isTop`, `leq` and `leqStrongMask` all join
the new channel (a prototype that skipped `isTop` was caught by the order matrix, per the note in the
carrier).  The plumbing that keeps it non-inert is `SpatialTypeSystem.constrainShape` and
`SpatialAnalysis.capWidth`, the two places outside `mk` that rebuild a `Shape` by hand.

MEASURED, key-disjoint union under a shared prefix:
    n     = 4 8 12 | 13 16 24 64 256 1024 4096
    before  [2,2]  | [2,15] [2,18] ... [2,4098]      (Θ(1) -> Θ(n) at MaxHeads + 1)
    after   [2,2]  | [2,2]  [2,2]  ... [2,2]         FLAT, derived |Q| = 2 at every n
and across the depth cap the d = MaxDepth+1 row went [5,9] -> [5,5] (exact).  Past MaxDepth+1 the
divergent keys are BELOW the collapsed level, where no certificate can help — that is the depth
budget, and the test now asserts the honest claim (exact to MaxDepth+1, linear in d past it) rather
than a discontinuity.  `SpatialShapeCheck`, `SpatialLawCheck`, `SpatialAnalysisCheck` and the γ-gate
stay green with the new channel enforced.
