## 2026-08-31 — acceptance-review resolution pass, round 2: the cost gate, the citation sweep, and the
## benchmark artifacts

ITEM 11 — THE COST GATE.  `SpatialCostCheck`'s WIDTH requirement went from 51 red rows to 41, every
one of them now carrying an evidence entry (it was 44 of 51, with 7 UNDIAGNOSED).  Per scenario, and
every number below is measured on the same 14-operator table with |a| = 64 over 8 heads and |b| = 16:

  range-part   trie/graph Touch 100.00 / 200.00 -> 6.00 / 6.00      RESOLVED
               zipper Work 99.00 -> 1.67, Alloc 110 -> 81, Touch 437 -> 85
  range-full   zipper Work 99.00 -> 1.67, Alloc 74 -> 74            (Work RESOLVED)
  fixpoint     Rounds 37.00 -> 1.50 on all three backends            RESOLVED
               trie Work 37.00 -> 1.50, graph Work 128.25 -> 4.00, zipper 1.43   RESOLVED
               Alloc 7447 -> 205, Touch 20367 -> 558.5               (still red; OP-1/OP-2's cause)
  iteration    graph Work 2425 -> 25, graph Alloc 669.5 -> 37        (Alloc RESOLVED)
               trie/zipper Work 437 / 401 -> 256 / 234, Touch 113    (still red)
  tails-union  trie/graph Work 1609 -> 939, zipper Alloc 74 -> 74    (still red)
  tails-inter  trie/graph Work 1609 -> 939, zipper Work 1806 -> 1136 (still red)

FOUR CORRECTIONS, in order of how much they moved:

(1) THE FIXPOINT ROUND BOUND WAS THREE SEPARATE BUGS, not a missing must-count.  `fixRounds` decided
    monotonicity with a two-case syntactic match on `Union(rec, _)` / `Union(_, rec)`, so the same
    accumulator RE-ASSOCIATED (`Union(Union(rec, a), b)`) was called non-monotone and fell straight
    to a FREE VARIABLE; it bounded the rounds by `|result| + 1` rather than `|result| - |init| + 1`
    (73 instead of 9); and it had no case for the shape that actually occurs — `Union(rec, E)` with
    `rec` NOT FREE in `E` makes the step IDEMPOTENT, so the loop runs ONE round to add `E` and one to
    observe that nothing changed, i.e. `[1, 2]` whatever the cardinalities are.  Now
    `fixRoundsIvl` returns an INTERVAL, the union tower is AC-flattened, the free-mention test is the
    binder-aware walk (a `Call`, a `GroundedSS` closure or a nested `Fixpoint` cannot hide an
    occurrence from it), and `Sym.monus` is a FOLD rather than a `Sym` case — a subtraction node
    would break the syntactic monotonicity `Sym.dominates` rests on.  Counted `FixpointRound` on the
    table's fixpoint: 2, predicted [1, 2].

(2) `execT` DOES NOT USE `joinAll` FOR A LOOP, AND THE MODEL SAID IT DID.  `GraphExec.scala`'s
    `case "Iteration"` is `var acc = ITrie.empty; src.children.foreach { … acc = ITrie.union(acc, …) }`
    — a PAIRWISE LEFT FOLD — while `GraphCost` inherited `TrieAlgebraCost.collectJoin`, which prices
    `evalI`'s n-ary `joinAll` including its operand probes and scratch slots.  Corrected, and the
    left fold is still LINEAR in the group count, not quadratic: `ITrie.union`'s descent follows only
    the keys present in BOTH operands, so one merge visits at most `min(nd(acc), nd(b_i)) <= nd(body)`
    however large the accumulator has grown.  Graph `Alloc` containment stayed 100% with median
    6.89 -> 3.02 and p95 31 -> 20.75; graph `Work` p95 13.02 -> 8.78.

(3) `naryProbes`' per-operand factor.  `min(k, 24) + 4` prices `collectLive`'s dedup as a FULL linear
    scan for EVERY operand, even past the `dedupScanMax = 24` threshold where it is a hash probe.
    Derived from the three loops in `IntTrieOps.joinAllTries` it is `dedup/k + 3` — 7 at k = 8
    against the previous 12, and against a counted amortised 2.4.

(4) Item 7's `Range` corrections (previous entry) closed `range-part` and `range-full` outright.

AND THE MUST SIDE COULD NOT BE BOUGHT.  `alloc` and the operand-loop half of `work` still start at 0
on every n-ary transfer, which is most of what is left.  TWO must-counts were derived and BOTH were
refuted by the counted oracle within one run: `4 + 3*kLo` scratch slots plus `kLo` probes took trie
`Alloc` containment 100% -> 98.5%, graph -> 94%, zipper -> 97.5%; the bare `ArrayBuffer(4)` that
`liveDistinct` allocates on entry took zipper `Alloc` -> 98%.  The reason is that `kLo` bounds the
HEADS while `liveDistinct` DEDUPS BY OBJECT IDENTITY — `{a.x, b.x}` builds ONE `{x}` trie and hangs
it under both keys, an unchanged branch of a fixpoint iterate is literally the previous round's
object, and `k` heads can collapse to ONE live operand, after which `joinAll` returns it by pointer
with no split arrays, no terminal scan and a probe count of zero.  Closing this needs a LIVE-OPERAND
count (how many head children are DISTINCT OBJECTS), which is per-head sub-shape information `Meas`
does not carry — the n-ary analogue of `SpatialFrontier`'s binary paired/reuse split.  That is
recorded as OP-6/OP-6g/OP-6z rather than guessed at, and OP-4/OP-5/OP-5g/OP-5z are RETIRED.
The zipper's `TailsIntersection` also taught the same lesson from the other side: it does materialise
and does call `ITrie.tailsIntersection`, but `merged` is a LAZY VAL, so a consumer that meets it with
∅ never forces it — the must claim produced an INVERTED interval (`actual=10 in [18, 16]`), which is
the unmistakable signature of charging for work that did not happen.
Containment after all of it: 97.33% (80 of 3000 corpus points) and 100% (66 cornerstone points) —
EXACTLY the numbers before this round, so nothing was tightened at soundness' expense.

ITEMS 9 AND 13 — THE DANGLING CITATIONS.  369 citations of a `review.md` that was never in the tree,
