     coverage test `n >= pairedAt(k)` derived from "every paired depth-k+1 prefix is a child of a
     paired depth-k prefix"), and `Pairing` gained `identicalAt` — POINTER IDENTITY BELOW THE ROOT,
     which is what interning makes common and what made seed 126 force one node too many: two equal
     leaf subtries under different prefixes ARE one object and the operator collapses there.  389
     programs, 241 with fully exact facts, all 241 exact on every counter.
  2. THE WIDTH SPILL'S NAMED KEYS WERE INVISIBLE TO THE WITNESS SEARCH.  `SpatialCheck.headItems`
     read `heads` and `otherTail` and not `otherKeys`, and `plan`'s walk therefore built a
     12-path "COMPLETE" set for a 16-head type and reported gamma EMPTY — an over-claim, not a
     shrug.  With the certificate read, `plan` returns 16 paths, the product query DECIDES the pair
     with a real witness, and the depth-capped shape needs NO fresh items at all (maxFresh = 0 no
     longer declines it).  Two tests moved to subjects that are genuinely open rather than merely
     un-enumerated, and the 16-head case is now a POSITIVE assertion.
  3. `SpatialLawsCheck` 11 was feeding the differential inputs the law is FALSE on.  `always` puts
     the law at EVERY node including the bare Mention, so the premise is "M denotes {q}" and not
     merely "the union does"; the old residual `Literal({q})` happened to agree on `M = 0` as well,
     which is what made the weaker filter look sufficient until the frontier became a rewrite
     consumer and the residual became `M`.
  4. `OptimalTrieCheck`'s distribution sweep was ALIGNMENT-SENSITIVE and silently so.  Every layout
     claim in it ("one high id block apart", "power-of-two ALIGNED blocks") is a claim about the
     interned ids' BIT structure, and the base id depends on how much of the rest of the suite
     interned first — so five rows that must read a flat 2 oscillated 4,2,2,4,2 as soon as the
     fuzzer's new operators shifted the interner.  `alignIds` pads to a power-of-two boundary; the
     rows are flat at every aligned base and the fixture now says so.
