`EquivPipelineTest` is the tree's largest artifact producer: 98 files (55 egg under
`zipper-egg-tests/pipeline`, 42 SMT plus a STATUS.tsv under `proofs/pipeline`).  Its first VERIFY run
under 0.3's sink reported 54 of the 98 as CHANGED, from TWO causes, and only one of them is staleness:

  1. THE INTERNER IDS, again, and this time inside the SMT goals themselves:

         committed:  (define-fun s_2 ((p Path)) Bool (or (= p (cons 12302 (cons 12303 nil))) ...
         produced:   (define-fun s_2 ((p Path)) Bool (or (= p (cons 15 (cons 16 nil))) ...

     Five-digit ids where a suite that owns its JVM produces two-digit ones — which is also the whole
     of the size difference (2410 B -> 2206 B on datalog-sn-graph.smt2).  Same root cause as the 20
     egg artifacts above, now shown to reach the PROVER OBLIGATIONS as well as the egg programs.
     Regenerating fixes it, and 0.2's per-suite JVM is what keeps it fixed.

  2. PROVER WALL-CLOCK IN A COMMITTED ARTIFACT, which no regeneration can fix.  The header line read

         ; forall-path goal   z3 unsat   9 ms   vampire refutation   6 ms (budget 60s each)

     and the milliseconds differ on every run (`6 ms` vs `7 ms`; `60012 ms` vs `60491 ms` on the
     timeouts).  Twelve of the 42 SMT artifacts were therefore UNSTABLE BY CONSTRUCTION: a
     golden-file gate over them could never be green, and a gate that can never be green is a gate a
     reader learns to ignore.  This is the same defect, in the same shape, as the `OPTIMIZED in
     836 ms` figure that sat inside `SpatialEventsCheck`'s `CALIBRATION:` channel.

     FIXED AT THE EMITTER, not by a filter in the comparator.  The header now carries both VERDICTS
     and the BUDGET — the two facts a reader of a proof artifact acts on, and `timeout` already says
     the budget was exhausted — and the timings are PRINTED per obligation, so the run log, which is
     where a performance question belongs, still has them.  A filter list in the comparator was the
     alternative and it is the wrong one: it grows silently until the gate compares nothing.

WHAT THE SINK IS WORTH, stated as a measurement rather than a claim.  Across six suites it found:
