    Matching.subst / subst2            -> Subst.apply / Subst.path
    EquivPipeline.substMention         -> Subst.mention
    EquivPipeline.substPathRef         -> Subst.pathRef
    EquivPipeline's Lower.inline (x2)  -> Subst.apply, ONE call with BOTH maps
    MORKL's IterateLiteral_Union       -> Subst.apply
    MORKL's IterateSingleton_Deref     -> Subst.apply (two arms)
    MORKL's asFixpointGeneral `sub`    -> Subst.mention
    SpatialRecursion.splice            -> Subst.apply

THREE SUBSTITUTION SITES THE PLAN DID NOT NAME, found by sweeping `subs` for substitution-shaped
uses.  All three are now routed, and one of them was a live capture hazard:

  * `SizeConstraints`' alpha-renamer (3 sites).  Correct today, but only BY ACCIDENT OF ORDER: `go(b)`
    runs first and bottom-up, so every inner binder has already been renamed to a fresh `~m`/`~p` and
    there is nothing left to shadow.  That argument was nowhere written down and evaporates the
    moment the pass is made top-down.
  * `SpatialPipeline.iterationSubstitute`.  The `rebinds` guard refuses the rewrite when the template
    REBINDS `sym`/`rest`, which handles SHADOWING by refusal — but capture is the OTHER direction and
    `rebinds` cannot see it.  The replacement is `TailsUnion(src)`, which is NOT closed, so a binder
    inside `tmpl` named after a free name of `src` captured it.  The header said "the substitution
    would then capture", describing shadowing; the two are separate hazards and it had only one.
  * `SpatialPipeline.unrollProvedHeads`.  Closed replacements, so never a capture hazard — routed so
    that there is only one substitution and so `rebinds` stops being what correctness rests on.

`SubstCapture` (13 tests) supplies what `SubstConformance` structurally cannot: OPEN replacements.
Capture at all six binders (Iteration's `symbol`/`rest`, Fixpoint's `rec`, Fold's `acc`/`symbol`/
`rest`), shadowing as its mirror, hint preservation across a rename, and `g(y,x)` end to end through
`unrollControl` itself.  GATE GREEN: `SubstConformance` 4, `SubstCapture` 13, `AlphaNormCheck` 7.

