     unbounded untracked count — so `Unwrap` could not be shown to select a single tile.
  4. THE INFORMATION EXISTS AND IS DESTROYED, not absent.  `Sliding.superpose`'s per-cell arm types
     EXACTLY: `{c0?{_?{ε}}, c1?{+[1,1] more}, …}`, size `[13, 28]`, ONE tile per cell.

Four independent losses sat between (4) and (3), and three of them are now fixed:

  * `Shape.tailsUnion` opened the untracked bucket's counts unconditionally.  With at most ONE
    untracked head there is no aggregation and nothing to open (`Shape.untrackedTails`).
  * `groupTailType`/`ChainCost.leafEnv` installed `SpatialType.top` per level.  They now install the
    per-level FIBER BOUND, and where the source has exactly one head (`headCount == [1,1]`) they
    install it UN-weakened — the single-group exemption, which is sound because "in some group's
    tails" and "in this group's tails" are then the same claim.
  * `SpatialTyping.groupUnion` bounded the group count only by the shape's `headCount`, which is
    capped at `shapeDepth = 4` levels.  The PATH COUNT bounds it too and the length histogram has no
    depth cap, so a 15-item singleton source is now known to have one group at every level.  The
    `Call` arm also threw the argument's length type away (`SpaceType.unknown`) and no longer does.
    MEASURED: `superpose`'s arm went from `[0, 241]` with `+[0,16]` tiles per cell to `[0, 28]` with
