ONE PREFIX, NOT THEIR UNION: `Shape.maxTailSize` (plan.md 1B.5, and it helps far beyond it)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`Unwrap(x, p)` with `|p| = j` KNOWN selects the tail-set under ONE depth-`j` prefix.  Every bound the
domain had for it was a bound on the UNION over prefixes: `Shape.unwrapUnknown` returns
`weaken(tailsUnion(x))`, whose cardinality is the SUM of the per-head tail-sets, and `SpatialTypes`'
`Unwrap` arm keeps the whole source's size class-by-class.  Both are sound and both answer about the
wrong object.

`Shape.maxTailSize(j)` is the right one — the LARGEST tail-set under any depth-`j` prefix, taking the
untracked bucket's contribution from `otherTail`'s own size (channel (d) is a PER-HEAD claim, so
`others.hi` does not multiply it) and `Ivl.INF` when there is no summary to read.  `SpatialCost`'s
`Unwrap` arm meets it into `Meas.size` whenever `plen` is a known constant in `1..MaxDepth`.

MEASURED on the cornerstone ledger, `Routine.optimized`, trie backend:

               alloc  before      after        touch  before      after
    gol               2.654e+04   6.707e+03           9.039e+04   2.665e+04     4.0x / 3.4x
    puzzle15          7.610e+55   1.017e+54           2.581e+56   3.449e+54      75x /  75x
    reference gol     1.896e+04   5.228e+03           7.336e+04   1.763e+04     3.6x / 4.2x

aunt, temperature, nqueens4 and datalog-sn are unchanged — they have no `Unwrap` by a known-length
path over a multi-head source, which is exactly the shape of term the law is about.

IT DOES NOT CLOSE puzzle15, and the reason says where the remaining factor is.  All fifteen factors of
`Sliding.collapse`'s `Composition` are `Unwrap(ass, Constant(c_i))` with `j = 1`, and `ass`'s per-head
tail-sets are each bounded at 3.8e10 — so `maxTailSize(1)` is 3.8e10 there and `tighter` keeps the
3584 the length histogram already gave.  The 75x came from OTHER `Unwrap` nodes in the same term
(`map(l)`, `state(...)`) where the max really is below the sum.  puzzle15 needs `ass`'s per-head bound,
which is the composition `map(l) x t` recorded above as 1B.5's remaining target.
